  %% Target design: swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-task-vm-sweep.yaml, docs/reference/compute-drivers.md#sweep-upcloud, docs/cli/README.md design rules R2-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02 (second pass), rules 14 (no `format` or `result` steps and no root `format`; the Gateway reads the plan step and the run's step statuses), 9 (one read-back and one native `assert`), 18 (one workflow; removals parallel forEach, server and template deletes one forEach). Reduced to UpCloud on 2026-11-07: an Incus host has no sweep, because a failed start is released by `task_vm.slot_release` (docs/cli/tasks/vm-release.mmd).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · scheduled sweep every 30 minutes
  %% kind: task_vm.sweep_host
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane UC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant UC as UpCloud API<br/>HTTPS from 209
  Note over GW: Admit the sweep<br/>Gateway Node · task #5182
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `SweepTaskVmHosts`, queued every 30 minutes while task VMs are on or the UpCloud token is set; the same job releases the task VMs that a failed start left on an Incus host
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - UpCloud is configured; no open sweep of the Gateway Node, and the generic Operation lock holds it until the terminal result
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the ownership scope: the live UpCloud VM names, the maximum VM id and the stamps of the template builds that run
  %%> - touches no Incus host: the sweep holds no host lock and carries no host input
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-sweep
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `operation_id`, `node_id`, `kind`, the full public `intent` with the scope
  %%> - the vault key name `task-vm-upcloud-token` only (R3)
  SW->>UC: List servers, templates<br/>inventory · curl on 209
  %%> How:
  %%> - one inline `curl` per list, the token through `--variable`, never argv: servers labelled `orbit-task-vm` and `orbit-task-image`, and storage templates
  Note over SW: Plan the cloud removals<br/>plan · task-vm-sweep-input
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - selects servers without a live row, build servers and unverified templates older than two hours, except a build still marked running
  SW->>UC: Stop started servers<br/>stop-server · forEach
  %%> How:
  %%> - a hard stop per started server, in parallel
  SW->>UC: Delete servers, templates<br/>remove · forEach
  %%> How:
  %%> - one parallel `forEach`: each server with its storage, each unverified template
  %%> Retry:
  %%> - UpCloud refuses a server that is still stopping; the next sweep deletes it
  SW->>UC: List again<br/>inventory · curl on 209
  %%> How:
  %%> - the same three lists
  SW->>SW: Check the cloud removals<br/>assert
  %%> End check:
  %%> - a native `assert`: no planned server or template UUID is still listed
  alt sweep complete
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run once; it takes the plan step's names
    Note over GW: Project the sweep<br/>missing VMs
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a `ready` or `parked` UpCloud VM missing on two sweeps in a row becomes `failed` with `task_vm.vm_missing`, and its group asks for assistance
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the sweep failed<br/>no missing-VM count
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5182 fails with `task_vm.host_command_failed`
    %%> - a provider failure never counts as a missing VM; the next sweep runs again in 30 minutes
  end
